"modification": "Replacement of the terminal methyl group on the butyl chain with a methyl group",
"rationale": "The butyl chain likely contributes to lipophilicity and may be involved in hydrophobic interactions. Replacing the terminal methyl group with a larger methyl group could increase the lipophilicity and potentially improve binding affinity. This modification is synthetically straightforward, involving a Grignard reaction with methylmagnesium bromide followed by reduction."
